name luatex
category TLCore
revision 78218
shortdesc The LuaTeX engine
longdesc LuaTeX is a greatly extended version of pdfTeX using Lua as an
longdesc embedded scripting language. The LuaTeX project's main
longdesc objective is to provide an open and configurable variant of TeX
longdesc while at the same time offering substantive backward
longdesc compatibility. LuaTeX uses Unicode (as UTF-8) as its default
longdesc input encoding, and is able to use modern (OpenType and
longdesc TrueType) fonts (for both text and mathematics).
